==In the manga==
[[File:Evelyn Adventures.png|150px|thumb|Evelyn in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
===Pokémon Adventures===
Evelyn debuted in ''[[PS582|Pinsir Glares]]''. At the shore of [[Kiloude City]], the Battle Chatelaines found an unconscious {{adv|Blaine}}, who was injured after being sent flying by the firing of the [[ultimate weapon]]. They took Blaine to the [[Battle Maison]] and allowed him to rest and recuperate there. Later, in ''[[PS587|Malamar Traps]]'', Evelyn and her sisters saw a recovered Blaine off.
{{-}}

==In the TCG==
[[File:EvelynTeamUp141.jpg|200px|thumb|{{TCG ID|Team Up|Evelyn|141}} in the TCG]]
Evelyn, as with the rest of the Battle Chatelaines, received a card in {{TCG|Team Up}}. Evelyn's card, {{TCG ID|Team Up|Evelyn|141}}, allows the player to draw four cards. However, it can only be played if the opponent's Active Pokémon is a Stage 1 Pokémon. The card can also be discarded as part of the cost for playing {{TCG ID|Team Up|Morgan|149}}, the card of the eldest Battle Chatelaine.
